[META]
framework: claude-framework
file_id: delegation.PATTERNS
class: universal
version: 1.0.0

[PATTERNS]
overview: Copy-paste-ready Agent() invocation templates for the most common delegation scenarios
usage: Pick the pattern matching your trigger; fill in the placeholders; ship.

[PATTERN_1_WIDE_EXPLORE]
when: Trigger 1 fires (orientation, wide reading)
template:
  Agent({
    description: "Explore <topic>",
    subagent_type: "Explore",
    prompt: "Find and summarize how <topic> works in this repo.
             Start from: <hint path or keyword>.
             Report: architecture summary + the 3-5 most relevant file:line citations.
             Under 250 words."
  })
notes:
  - Omit `model` — Explore has its own default
  - Always give a seed (keyword, path, or symbol) to avoid cold-start drift
  - Enforce word budget; otherwise Explore will return full file dumps

[PATTERN_2_DISTILL_LARGE_OUTPUT]
when: Trigger 2 fires (large output, only summary needed)
template:
  Agent({
    description: "<verb> <object>",
    subagent_type: "general-purpose",
    model: "haiku",
    prompt: "Run <exact command> and report ONLY: <exact shape>.
             Do not include raw output. Do not include reasoning.
             If the command fails, report the single error line and exit code."
  })
example:
  prompt: "Run `npm test` in ./packages/api. Report: total tests, passed, failed.
           If any failed, list failing test names (one per line) with the first error line each.
           Nothing else."

[PATTERN_3_PARALLEL_INDEPENDENT]
when: Trigger 3 fires (2+ independent subtasks)
template: Send ONE message with MULTIPLE Agent() blocks
example:
  Message contains:
    Agent({description: "Audit Website deps", ...})
    Agent({description: "Audit RenderEngine deps", ...})
    Agent({description: "Audit IllustratorPlugIn deps", ...})
notes:
  - All three run concurrently
  - Each gets its own word budget
  - Main agent synthesizes after all return

[PATTERN_4_MECHANICAL_TRANSFORM]
when: Trigger 4 fires (mechanical task)
template:
  Agent({
    description: "<verb> <object>",
    subagent_type: "general-purpose",
    model: "haiku",
    prompt: "In files <exact paths>, <exact transformation>.
             Follow this pattern exactly (copy from <reference file>): <pattern or example>.
             Do not redesign. Do not add comments. Do not change unrelated code.
             Confirm by listing the files changed and line counts."
  })
example:
  prompt: "In files src/api/v1/*.ts, add a `@deprecated` JSDoc tag above every exported function.
           Pattern: /** @deprecated Use v2 instead. */.
           Do not modify function bodies. List changed files + count of tags added."

[PATTERN_5_PLAN_REFACTOR]
when: Trigger 5 fires (multi-file planning)
template:
  Agent({
    description: "Plan <refactor>",
    subagent_type: "Plan",
    prompt: "Design an implementation plan for: <goal>.
             Current state: <one or two sentences + key file paths>.
             Constraints: <list>.
             Return: ordered step list, critical files, risks. No code."
  })

[PATTERN_6_OPEN_SEARCH]
when: Trigger 6 fires (unclear target)
template:
  Agent({
    description: "Locate <thing>",
    subagent_type: "general-purpose",
    prompt: "Find <thing> in this repo.
             It may be called: <synonyms / likely names>.
             It is likely in: <plausible locations>.
             Return: exact file:line of the definition + 1-sentence explanation.
             If not found after reasonable search, say so explicitly."
  })

[PATTERN_7_ISOLATED_RISKY_EDIT]
when: Edit touches shared state or may break main branch; user wants to validate before merging
template:
  Agent({
    description: "<task>",
    subagent_type: "general-purpose",
    isolation: "worktree",
    prompt: "<task brief> ..."
  })
notes:
  - Worktree is auto-cleaned if no changes made
  - If changes made, path + branch are returned for review
  - Use for: experimental refactors, destructive migrations, anything reversible-but-scary

[PATTERN_8_BACKGROUND_WORK]
when: Subtask is long-running AND main agent has other independent work to progress
template:
  Agent({
    description: "<task>",
    run_in_background: true,
    prompt: "..."
  })
notes:
  - Do NOT poll — completion arrives as a notification
  - Good for: long test suites, wide scans, multi-file refactors where you can keep working

[PROMPT_BRIEFING_CHECKLIST]
Every spawned subagent prompt MUST contain:
  1. What to do (verb + object)
  2. Relevant context (why, constraints, existing state — enough to act without this conversation)
  3. Exact output shape (format + length cap)
  4. What NOT to do (especially for mechanical / haiku tasks)

If any of the four is missing, the prompt is not ready.
